title: Soviet Election Campaign
card-image: img/cards/campaigning.svg?v=2
subtitle: Contest the factory and city soviets.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: campaigning_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; campaigning_timer = 3

[? if bol_regime = 0 and dix < 20 : Soviets are re-elected often, sometimes every month, and a deputy who displeases his factory is recalled at the next meeting. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix < 30 : The soviets were re-elected after October with the Bolsheviks counting the votes, but some factories still send back the deputies of other parties. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 30 and dix < 44 : The soviets are being re-elected one town at a time, and where the opposition wins, a detachment from Moscow is apt to arrive and dissolve the result. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 44 and dix < 96 : Elections are held by a show of hands, with the Communist cell's list read out first and the Cheka's man at the door. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 96 : The Moscow Soviet is re-elected this spring. The party's candidates will stand, those of them who are not already in prison. ?][? if bol_regime = 0 and dix >= 20 : Under the Republic the soviets compete with the elected town dumas and the zemstvos, and a campaign must be fought in both. ?] A campaign costs money for printing, halls and travel. [? if resources < 1 : We have nothing to spend. ?]

- @factories: Campaign in the factories. (1 resource)
- @garrisons: Campaign in the garrisons and at the front. (1 resource)
- @railways: Campaign among the railwaymen and postal workers. (1 resource)
- @joint: A joint list with our bloc partner. (1 resource)
- @villages: Campaign in the villages. (1 resource)
- @speeches: Send speakers out with no printed material.
- @easy_discard

@villages
view-if: player_party = 'sr' or player_party = 'lsr'
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 7, soldiers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

[? if bol_regime = 0 or dix < 36 : Speakers went out to the volost assemblies and the village gatherings. The peasants listen to the party that calls itself their own. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 36 : Speakers went out to the volost assemblies by the back roads, past the posts of the requisition squads. The peasants listen to the party that calls itself their own, when nobody from the town is watching. ?]

@speeches
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, railway: 1});
!}

Without money for leaflets, the speakers went out on their own. It was not much of a campaign, but it was a campaign.

@factories
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6});
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1});
!}

[? if bol_regime = 0 : Every shop floor that elects its deputies hears our speakers first. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 : Every shop floor that still votes heard our speakers first, before the Communist cell could read out its list. ?]

@garrisons
choose-if: resources >= 1 and bol_regime = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 1 : We have no resources. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 : There is no garrison left that we may enter. ?]
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 6});
Q.militia = (Q.militia || 0) + 0.5;
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

The soldiers' committees are less patient than the workers', but they still listen to the Soviet's own party.

@railways
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {railway: 7, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, 0);
!}

The railwaymen and the telegraph clerks have their own union and their own politics. They trust the party that listens to them.

@joint
view-if: ally_lvl >= 2 or ally_lsr >= 2
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, soldiers: 5, peasants: 3, railway: 3});
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 1);
!}

A joint list showed one democracy instead of two parties. The Bolsheviks called it a deal between bureaucrats.
